    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "exactly. so if the system basically just serves as a tool for managing risks and lets big powers stall things, isn't it kind of a lost cause when it comes to actually protecting smaller countries? it seems like the \"global governance\" model is just a massive illusion that hides the fact that real power still just works through force or leverage. do you think there's any real benefit to sticking with it, or is it just a failed experiment at this point?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
